soc: sunxi: h713-arisc: run the EDID sequence once more when the display MIPS cut into it

crust serves the display MIPS's frames in the same pass as this driver's
commands, and this driver's lock only orders ARM callers. A hotplug
frame (0x16) or a module reset (0x17) between two steps of the EDID
sequence changes what the next one finds - a reset clears the store and
the gate between two fragments, a hotplug "down" during the pulse
satisfies its counter with the pin left low - and the receiver's probe
fails on the first, or succeeds on the second with the source left
without a hotplug edge.

crust counts both frames (contract 5, CNT1[31:16]). When the sequence
failed and the count moved while it ran, it runs once more, with a
warning. A sequence that succeeded is not repeated, frames or not, only
named in an info line with the two counts: a second run would give the
source a second hotplug pulse, and should the MIPS answer the sequence's
own pulse with a frame, every probe and every reload would run twice.
At probe, an edge a frame may have cost comes back with the receiver's
own pulse at the end of its bring-up. How often the MIPS sends either in
normal use is not measured; the info line is where to count it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-arisc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-arisc.c
@@ -2735,14 +2735,12 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(arisc_hdmi_hpd);
  * probe time and splitting it across the callers would invite reordering --
  * the order is not a convention, it is what the firmware accepts.
  */
-int arisc_hdmi_edid_init(unsigned int port, const void *edid, size_t len)
+static int arisc_edid_sequence(struct h713_arisc *a, unsigned int port,
+			       const void *edid, size_t len)
 {
-	struct h713_arisc *a = arisc_get(false);
 	u8 readback[ARISC_HDMI_EDID_BLOCK];
 	int ret;
 
-	if (IS_ERR(a))
-		return PTR_ERR(a);
 	if (port >= ARISC_HDMI_PORTS)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
@@ -2797,6 +2795,45 @@ int arisc_hdmi_edid_init(unsigned int port, const void *edid, size_t len)
 	dev_info(a->dev, "EDID/HPD sequence on port %u completed\n", port);
 	return 0;
 }
+
+/*
+ * The display MIPS talks to crust as well, and a hotplug frame (0x16) or a
+ * module reset (0x17) of its between two steps of the sequence changes what
+ * the next step finds: a cleared EDID store, a pin pulled low. crust counts
+ * both (contract 5, CNT1[31:16]); a sequence that failed while they cut in
+ * is run once more, with a warning, rather than failing the receiver's
+ * probe on it. One that succeeded is not repeated: the source would see a
+ * second hotplug pulse, and the MIPS may well answer the sequence's own.
+ */
+static u16 arisc_mips_frames(struct h713_arisc *a)
+{
+	if (!a->off.crust || crust_rd(a, H713_VERSION) < 5)
+		return 0;
+	return crust_rd(a, H713_CNT1) >> 16;
+}
+
+int arisc_hdmi_edid_init(unsigned int port, const void *edid, size_t len)
+{
+	struct h713_arisc *a = arisc_get(false);
+	u16 mips, now;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (IS_ERR(a))
+		return PTR_ERR(a);
+
+	mips = arisc_mips_frames(a);
+	ret = arisc_edid_sequence(a, port, edid, len);
+	now = arisc_mips_frames(a);
+	if (ret && now != mips) {
+		dev_warn(a->dev, "the EDID sequence failed (%d) while the display MIPS sent hotplug or reset frames (0x%04x -> 0x%04x) -- running it once more\n",
+			 ret, mips, now);
+		ret = arisc_edid_sequence(a, port, edid, len);
+	} else if (now != mips) {
+		dev_info(a->dev, "the display MIPS sent hotplug or reset frames during the EDID sequence (0x%04x -> 0x%04x), not repeated\n",
+			 mips, now);
+	}
+	return ret;
+}
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(arisc_hdmi_edid_init);
 
